    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **62 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `Idempotency-Key` support for `POST /api/owners` following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection idiom (no `@RestController`, escalation-based branching rather than `@Flow`, transaction governance on every step).\n\n**New pieces:**\n\n1. **`IdempotencyStore`** (`@Component`) \u2014 a process-wide in-memory map of `Idempotency-Key \u2192 owner id`.\n\n2. **`CheckIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 new first step in the pipeline. Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header via `ServerHttpConnection`; if the key was already seen and its owner still exists (and isn't soft-deleted), it throws `IdempotentReplayException` carrying that owner, short-circuiting before the `EnsureUniqueIdentity` step (which would otherwise 409). No header, or an unseen key \u2192 the normal create pipeline proceeds.\n\n3. **`IdempotentReplayException`** + **`IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler`** + escalation YAML \u2014 the handler maps the carried owner to an `OwnerDto` and responds **200 OK**, mirroring the existing escalation pattern.\n\n4. **`RecordIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 new step after `audit` (once the owner has its id), records `key \u2192 owner.getId()` so a repeat replays.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: `idempotency` inserted as the entry step (`next: validate`), and `recordIdempotency` inserted between `audit` and `respond`.\n\nThe `Cp50Tests.coreIdempotentRepeat` test now passes: the first create returns 2xx with an id, the repeat with the same key returns 200 with the *same* id, and no duplicate is created.",
