    "probe_text": "I've read the entire pipeline. Here is the complete ordered trace.\n\n## POST /api/owners \u2014 ordered validations & side-effects\n\n**Gate (before any step):** the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Every step runs under one `transaction` governance, committing once at the end.\n\n| # | Step (class) | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | *auth* | Rejects unless caller has role `OWNER_ADMIN`. |\n| 1 | **CheckIdempotentCreate** | *Side-effect/short-circuit.* If an `Idempotency-Key` header is present and already maps to a still-existing, non-deleted owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 replays that owner as **200** (skips the rest). Otherwise proceeds. |\n| 2 | **ValidateOwnerFields** | *Validation + normalization.* Runs `OwnerAddresses.applyTo` (normalizes structured `addressLine1/2` or flat `address`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET/RD\u2192ROAD/AVE\u2192AVENUE; composes the flat `address`). Then requires `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` all present/non-blank \u2192 **400** `MissingOwnerFieldsException` listing each missing field. Publishes the validated body for later steps. |\n| 3 | **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** | *Validation + normalization.* Converts telephone to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; `+` keeps country code, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`). Must be 8\u201315 digits; enforces national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 **400** `InvalidTelephoneException`. Mutates the body. |\n| 4 | **NormalizeOwnerEmail** | *Validation + normalization.* Email optional; if present it must be syntactically valid \u2192 else **400** `InvalidEmailException`; lower-cases it in place. |\n| 5 | **RejectDisposableEmailDomain** | *Validation.* If email present and its domain is on the blocklist (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 **400** `DisposableEmailDomainException`. |\n| 6 | **DeriveHouseholdId** | *Compute.* Derives `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized `(lastName, postcode)`; `null` if no postcode. Publishes it. |\n| 7 | **EnsureUniqueIdentity** | *Validation (409).* Against all non-deleted owners: rejects if `identityKey` (`telephone\\|email\\|householdId`) matches an existing owner (always), or if `householdId` matches an existing owner **unless** request declares `sharesHousehold`. \u2192 **409** `DuplicateIdentityException`. |\n| 8 | **EnsureCityCapacity** | *Validation (409).* Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 **50** \u2192 **409** `CityAtCapacityException`. |\n| 9 | **EnsureDailyOwnerLimit** | *Validation (429).* Computes the effective business-day registration date (supplied or today, weekends rolled to Monday); if \u2265 **100** owners already registered that business day \u2192 **429** `DailyOwnerLimitException`. |\n| 10 | **BuildOwner** | *Side-effect.* Maps the validated DTO to a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`; publishes it. |\n| 11 | **ValidateOwnerPostcode** | *Validation.* Postcode optional; if present must be 4 digits, and if the owner's **city** maps to a region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) must fall in that range \u2192 else **400** `InvalidPostcodeException`. |\n| 12 | **AssignHousehold** | *Side-effect.* Stamps the derived `householdId` onto the owner (if any). |\n| 13 | **AssignHouseholdSize** | *Side-effect.* Sets `householdSize` = 1 + existing owners with same non-null `householdId` (1 if no household). |\n| 14 | **ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate** | *Validation.* If a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 **400** `FutureRegistrationDateException`. |\n| 15 | **DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate** | *Side-effect.* Sets `registrationDate` = supplied-or-today, adjusted to a business day (weekend \u2192 next Monday). |\n| 16 | **AssignBulkSignupWarning** | *Side-effect.* Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > **80** owners already registered on that business day (excludes this one). |\n| 17 | **AssignCustomerCode** | *Side-effect.* Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from locality/city/UNKNOWN; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`), de-duplicated with `-<n>` (n\u22652) on collision with an existing code. |\n| 18 | **AssignNamesakeCount** | *Side-effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing firstName+lastName (case-insensitive), excluding this one. |\n| 19 | **AssignMembershipNumber** | *Side-effect.* Sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = fiscal year (starts 1 July) of the adjusted registration date. |\n| 20 | **DetectPossibleDuplicate** | *Side-effect.* Sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: true (lowest matching id) when a non-deleted existing owner shares `lastName`+`postcode`, different household, and a different `telephone`; else false. |\n| 21 | **SaveOwner** | *Side-effect.* Persists the owner (assigns its id). |\n| 22 | **AuditOwnerCreated** | *Side-effect.* Logs one line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber); read-only. |\n| 23 | **RecordIdempotentCreate** | *Side-effect.* If an `Idempotency-Key` header was present, records key \u2192 new owner id in `IdempotencyStore` (for future replays). |\n| 24 | **RespondWithOwnerCreated** | *Side-effect.* Maps owner to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. |\n\n### Notes worth flagging\n- **Validations (in order they can reject):** auth (403) \u2192 idempotent replay (200 short-circuit) \u2192 missing required fields (400) \u2192 telephone format (400) \u2192 email format (400) \u2192 disposable email domain (400) \u2192 duplicate identity/household (409) \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429) \u2192 postcode (400) \u2192 future registration date (400).\n- **Ordering quirk:** `DeriveHouseholdId` (step 6) and `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (step 7) read `request.getPostcode()`, but postcode format is only validated later at step 11 (`ValidateOwnerPostcode`). So an invalid postcode is used for household derivation/duplicate detection before it's rejected \u2014 though because everything runs in one transaction, a 400 at step 11 rolls the whole thing back."
